rs and twenty one years respectively after the record came into existence.\n26. Protection of information relating to privacy of the person\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), an information officer may refuse a request for access if its disclosure\nwould involve the unreasonable disclosure of personal information about a person, including a\ndeceased individual.\n(2) A person shall be granted access to a record referred to in subsection (1) in so far as the record\nconsists of information —\n(a) about a person who has consented in writing to its disclosure to the person requesting the\nrecord;\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 10','3d6fb4002603a83bb1aec5db0ce459a91948a1baa69d5b014974edd95bcda666','Access to Information Act — Chapter 95','General','[-0.0779152,0.08582818,-0.060518853,-0.02691249,-0.002718095,0.028780293,0.019529648,-0.05122568,0.043879785,0.03603834,0.016553266,0.0110111665,0.036701422,-0.049853586,-0.02450435,-0.06099718,0.026520602,0.017134111,-0.09838394,0.041049354,0.0911267,0.08310612,0.022790914,-0.0056937197,-0.050080795,-0.024622615,-0.04649609,-0.045097303,0.020063259,-0.007949835,0.048598047,8.0344226E-4,0.04573155,0.01748476,0.041400053,0.021696,-0.027465526,0.036423627,-0.005167149,-0.021646,-3.264589E-4,-0.03193691,0.007825631,0.029139176,-0.002165258,0.06484755,0.0506672,-0.014859415,-0.1221249,0.03487175,-0.07931654,0.018689869,0.014892001,0.070601776,-0.068795875,-0.02046073,-0.01655238,-0.02244479,-0.0722077,0.0141406795,-0.07486687,-0.03572399,-0.0057247723,-0.031226683,-0.052409712,0.017529028,0.040306553,-0.0048319576,0.052194305,1.05982035E-5,0.011566118,-0.03495342,-0.060550664,0.0353241,-0.026009463,-0.0150065245,-0.0018442582,-0.006172008,0.0027052849,-0.10888323,0.031118717,0.037244774,0.098525494,-0.04180397,-0.059685227,-0.08695394,0.019969327,-0.0096053835,-0.0028640532,-0.06051151,0.06879638,-0.029432425,0.1385131,0.018327508,0.0036357949,-0.03129299,0.006696237,0.021666821,-0.023446027,0.052200675,-0.05