y or by an advocate in his or her\nown defence.\n(3) Where the sentence dealt with under this section has been passed by a magistrate’s court, the High\nCourt may inflict a greater punishment for the offence, which in the opinion of the High Court the\naccused has committed, than might have been inflicted by the court which imposed the sentence.\n(4) Nothing in this section shall be deemed to authorise the High Court to convert a finding of acquittal\ninto one of conviction; except that when any person is acquitted of the offence with which he or she\nwas charged but is convicted of another offence, whether charged with that other offence or not, the\nHigh Court may, if it reverses the finding of conviction, itself convert the finding of acquittal into\none of conviction.\n(5) Any person aggrieved by any finding, sentence or order made or imposed by a magistrate','78f0a6c3863b9e84011a87177aff28bb2df1e080e88773c5f12b550ce73afb7f','Criminal Procedure Code Act','General','[-0.054967087,0.090411246,0.014087691,-0.09261964,-0.050502133,0.0037253408,0.025646508,0.020208467,0.021991907,0.11193149,0.10967189,0.07698231,0.031158509,-0.09326055,0.0046195905,-0.0054591596,0.012990753,-5.549763E-4,-0.063374035,0.05242045,0.07199001,0.014789501,-0.001751593,0.017580997,-0.055781815,-0.02008056,-0.08353442,-0.004406257,0.016165577,-0.058758084,-6.053976E-4,0.061007716,0.035327524,0.03758539,-0.051399287,0.031862892,0.037381988,-0.048981287,0.041110475,-0.022280408,0.043836292,0.013051984,0.031430244,-0.0654977,0.0067739994,-0.034320466,-0.021006761,0.012399383,-0.10595855,-0.045400705,-0.09942107,-0.034080923,-0.029747054,0.050522804,-0.05511835,-0.07223121,0.012020594,-1.0810648E-4,0.029490339,0.01894847,-0.049948055,0.043291736,-0.0815815,-0.021902004,0.038575616,-0.10135641,0.08131309,-0.07332939,0.006891933,0.06727858,0.1003749,-0.044072308,0.03699578,0.033820003,-0.12469397,-0.011509083,0.016820624,0.012110474,-0.01243712,-0.039111324,0.008976606,-0.0024466836,0.045412883,-0