005455534]','','2026-08-29 13:08:42.121003',NULL,'Criminal Procedure Code Act.pdf',17,'Criminal Procedure Code Act.pdf','98f665136ddc930fc66dac3db348dc7f03cde3ad59bebe9a5616c4da8967f8c9','',46),(284,46,'Criminal Procedure Code Act (Chapter 122)  Uganda\n53. High Court order to be certified to lower court\nWhen a case is revised by the High Court, it shall certify its decision or order to the court by which the\nsentence or order revised was recorded or passed, and the court to which the decision or order is certified\nshall then make such orders as are conformable to the decision certified, and, if necessary, the record shall\nbe amended in accordance with the decision or order.\n54. Authority to sign on behalf of Director of Public Prosecutions\nWhere an appeal or an application for revision is made by the Director of Public Prosecutions, the notice\nor application, as the case may be, shall be signed by the Director of Public Prosecutions or by any other\nperson as he or she may authorise either generally or specifically for that purpose.\n55. Power to amend Schedule\nThe Minister responsible for finance may, by statutory instrument, with the approval of Cabinet, amend\nthe Schedule to this Act.\nSchedule (sections 1, 55)\nCurrency point\nA currency point is equivalent to twenty thousand shillings\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 15','78f0a6c3863b9e84011a87177aff28bb2df1e080e88773c5f12b550ce73afb7f','Criminal Procedure Code Act','General','[-0.049244396,0.082766704,-0.05359724,-0.07461071,-0.06790605,-0.0100629395,-0.009790649,0.019465448,0.024169067,0.10805166,0.040176876,0.0067550014,3.4096022E-4,-0.032531027,0.019242201,-0.058954116,-0.014258518,0.011657623,-0.024456441,0.08665278,0.09284715,0.037501957,-0.02247695,0.010342972,-0.034399483,0.006732514,-0.053703304,0.018297818,-0.0088929515,-0.06341078,0.030119745,0.028048232,0.044921633,0.0073335133,0.0162224,0.029521788,0.025732478,-0.004522996,0.05097659,-0.011290038,0.09553026,-0.074106