ction order\n(1) A protection order may, where appropriate—\n(a) prohibit the perpetrator from committing or enlisting the help of another person to commit\nan act of domestic violence;\n(b) direct the perpetrator to stay away from the premises or place where the victim resides or\nany part of the premises, if the prohibition is in the best interest of the victim;\n(c) prohibit the perpetrator from entering or approaching any place or premises where the\nvictim works, frequents, attends or any part of the premises or place;\n(d) direct the perpetrator to pay maintenance in respect of the victim\'s needs or the needs of any\nchild or dependent of the perpetrator, including necessaries;\n(e) award the temporary custody of any child or dependent of the perpetrator to any person or\ninstitution and regulate rights of access by the perpetrator to the child or dependant;\n(f) direct the perpetrator to afford the victim or any child or dependent of the victim, access to\ntheir place of residence and use of the facilities associated with it;\n(g) direct the perpetrator to do or omit to do any act or thing which the court considers\nnecessary or desirable for the well being of the victim or any child or dependant of','b17700fc18c3a4cdd7966c6c3465a4fbbbc3cbb0fcc9e73f02e19d29c93ec2f6','Domestic Violence Act','General','[-0.06394107,0.076814055,0.04732109,-0.045374222,0.0064744405,0.0580593,-0.006440005,-0.06782362,0.021770533,0.112263404,0.09805131,0.029678695,0.019760232,-0.039309327,0.015194713,-0.023664147,0.0765877,-0.045231152,-0.06644966,0.06435781,0.0692365,0.05116558,0.025859421,-0.009884129,-0.07352845,0.010400235,-0.014221097,0.0048072417,0.052326705,-0.061800525,0.003644801,-0.07903113,0.012813836,0.0406985,-0.07743036,0.004027365,0.043726362,-0.0445369,0.00941649,-0.057403464,0.022916082,-0.029797582,0.04222799,-0.12484565,-0.012460826,0.050584093,0.04985431,0.007166945,-0.06233708,-0.112023175,-0.033368878,-0.010035356,-0.030051015,0.12379591,-0.022235636,-0.06188