y the employer, produce a certificate as to her medical condition from a qualified\nmedical practitioner or midwife.\n56. Paternity leave\n(1) A male employee shall, immediately after the delivery or miscarriage by a wife, have the right to a\nperiod of four working days’ leave from work yearly herein referred to as paternity leave.\n(2) An employee referred to in subsection (1) shall be entitled to the payment of his full wages during\nthe said paternity leave.\n(3) A male employee shall, after the paternity leave, have the right to return to the job which he held\nimmediately before his paternity leave.\n56A. Establishment of breastfeeding and child care facilities\n(1) Every employer shall make available at the workplace, time, space or a facility for breastfeeding and\nchild care for children of the employees.\n(2) The facility referred to in subsection (1) shall be for children between the ages of three months and\nthirty-six months.\n(3) The Minister shall, by regulations, prescribe operational standards for the breastfeeding and child\ncare facilities referred to in subsection (1).\n[section 56A inserted by section 11 of Act 10 of 2026]\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 24','d1cc6c37d9f8420fad71d9e0bca366a6d1aaf3bbdda5cb69c9066fe0fdef38c0','Employment Act','General','[-0.06675008,0.04060409,0.010654779,-0.015267128,0.06924036,0.0964349,-0.072890215,0.056640714,-0.012001563,-0.0011348269,0.03252759,0.025578737,-0.06835202,-0.049820684,0.009285496,0.005950677,0.072755106,0.015156389,-0.007018191,0.017049737,0.09419652,-0.032073513,-0.012410688,-0.00416789,0.0775822,0.018052835,0.008284741,0.056321397,0.09202912,0.06140871,0.037873767,0.008502895,0.024796324,-0.09722421,-0.08908827,0.02796148,0.015180233,-0.011685124,0.044777993,0.012629234,-0.026332397,-0.03301846,0.02134066,0.034138065,0.005691269,0.05248437,-0.03555646,-0.02784116,-0.07714766,0.013907179,0.020336112,-0.06016146,-0.04607594,0.122162975,-0.07729256,-0.05282891,0.0098344395,