y.\n(2) For any or all of the information required by subsection (1), the employer may, in writing, refer\nthe employee to a document which is reasonably accessible to the employee during working hours\nat the place of work which contains the relevant information in a form and in a language that the\nemployee can reasonably be expected to understand.\n(3) The notice referred to in subsection (1) shall be given by the employer to the employee not later\nthan twelve weeks after the date on which employment commences.\n(4) Where there has been an agreed change affecting any of the matters referred to in subsection (1),\nthe employer shall issue a written notice to the employee of the change.\n(5) An employer shall retain a copy of the written particulars issued under subsection (1), and of any\nchanges in them and shall produce the copy on demand, to a labour officer.\n59. Written particulars to act as evidence\nWhere there is any dispute between an employer and employee concerning the terms and conditions of\nemployment—\n(a) the written particulars referred to in section 58, together with any notice of change, shall be\nadmissible evidence of the existence of the terms and conditions about which there is a dispute;\nand\n(b) there shall be a rebuttable presumption that the terms and conditions of employment are accurately\nstated in the written particulars and in any','d1cc6c37d9f8420fad71d9e0bca366a6d1aaf3bbdda5cb69c9066fe0fdef38c0','Employment Act','General','[-0.03175055,0.092508055,0.03795928,-0.012427439,0.028826058,0.059000958,0.029592274,0.0010661453,-0.040852074,0.040065072,0.046348445,0.016757831,-0.016576478,-0.07099484,0.0042361757,-0.046576276,-0.015109738,0.010047694,-0.03124246,0.04618312,0.096507594,0.10715555,-0.018174047,0.046990562,-0.025501408,0.017361183,2.1395004E-4,0.011244204,0.038324952,-0.01931545,-0.0301773,0.017983578,0.045861878,-0.0022928978,0.008892395,0.01899182,0.03550867,-0.020356191,-0.018366536,-0.07032147,7.0811575E-4,-0.03405531,0