sition of the penalty or suspension, make a written or oral complaint to a\nlabour officer.\n(2) Where a complaint under this section has been made to a labour officer, the officer shall—\n(a) investigate the circumstances leading to the imposition of the disciplinary penalty, and\nin the course of these investigations he or she shall consult any labour union, if any,\nestablished in the business in which the employee is employed; and\n(b) seek to settle the matter in the first instance by mediation.\n(3) Where a complaint under this section has been made, a labour officer shall, except where the\nemployer has withdrawn the disciplinary penalty imposed or has paid the employee for the period\nof the suspension, decide whether it was reasonable for the employer to impose the disciplinary\npenalty or the suspension with half pay.\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 27','d1cc6c37d9f8420fad71d9e0bca366a6d1aaf3bbdda5cb69c9066fe0fdef38c0','Employment Act','General','[-0.06182849,0.088649064,0.07597944,0.015337982,0.027539419,0.04244456,-0.024239844,-0.023308834,-0.03262024,0.101499386,0.051796433,-0.0820586,-0.02327743,-3.3056625E-4,-0.026283883,-0.0031876445,0.0035919275,0.062128685,-0.044797104,-0.011337491,0.12776192,-0.058139697,-0.074834,0.08865109,-0.019187784,-0.021664722,0.0070386413,0.052803177,0.032156434,-0.009150316,-0.062420487,0.005147073,-0.049069896,-0.02488992,-0.057669852,-0.027007185,0.099377476,0.008161453,-0.014920464,-0.041241333,0.03483884,0.04461995,-0.03370033,-0.013742594,0.05123431,-0.0055778273,0.068898745,0.016200991,-0.11109626,-0.01764829,0.007731853,-0.019553423,0.005072461,0.057802413,-0.097139634,-0.07098673,-6.315831E-4,-0.02736592,0.02277254,0.048213914,-0.06307361,-0.093935914,-0.022999942,0.011725488,0.009176171,-0.07488438,-0.043176338,-0.08493155,-0.0031049452,0.06624233,0.019673849,-0.08698291,0.011229333,0.012665443,-0.008382475,0.023481349,0.008794654,0.062279608,0.0051679797,-0.097466,0.049092695,-0.030242627,