17941497,0.13432062,-5.368839E-4,-1.9104086E-4,-0.017535463]','','2026-08-29 13:09:59.215941',NULL,'Hindu Marriage and Divorce Act #U2014 Chapter 145.pdf',6,'Hindu Marriage and Divorce Act #U2014 Chapter 145.pdf','912b7b9169849573b4ef81b8886dfdf85bcf84da9148b0ace51ab1de7d9dc2eb','',10),(592,10,'cree of nullity of marriage—\n(a) shall not be granted on the ground that the parties are within the prohibited degrees of\nconsanguinity if the custom governing each party permits a marriage between them;\n(b) in the case of a marriage solemnised before the commencement of this Act, shall not be\ngranted on the grounds that the former husband or wife of either party was living at the time\nof the marriage and the marriage with the previous husband or wife was then in force; and\n(c) may be granted on the ground that the consent of a guardian in marriage was necessary\nunder this Act and was obtained by force or fraud.\n(4) In this section, references to the Divorce Act include a reference to any Act replacing that Act.\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 4','550d730e6560f1cb258c26b6358c766454be15dd959a422a5a82982dd6948818','Hindu Marriage and Divorce Act #U2014 Chapter 145','General','[-0.09219587,0.06801864,-0.034220148,0.014502551,-0.007376275,0.0350346,0.031090714,-0.06489188,-0.017807143,0.120114654,0.052776992,0.0137804495,0.028959485,-0.020133803,0.025160016,0.035827044,-0.0022138348,-0.036687814,-0.044075307,0.13463551,0.05447613,0.049078036,0.002298068,0.03645509,0.030431058,-0.04306459,-0.03071257,0.0032224536,0.031692367,-0.037793435,0.040019106,0.12501732,0.0056717177,0.08807859,-0.021848556,-0.06667895,-0.02869421,0.044938575,0.018719366,-0.057900127,0.10646901,0.037603825,0.022847787,-0.044585437,-0.029253548,0.052355126,-0.018446159,-0.026465014,-0.10372544,5.105377E-4,-0.040174257,-0.0020254962,-0.032830026,0.087697566,0.06980872,-0.06331026,-0.02363928,-0.07348601,0.04120518,0.04721455,0.05344287,0.055696804,-0.035185985,-0.02130321,0.05096