9,-0.015274851,0.069095075,-0.03888009,-0.05695086,-0.009879429,0.0063214703,0.05590422,-0.015811509,0.03390946,-0.029641513,0.011685287,0.0026120157,0.072519846,0.01980695,0.088372275,-0.07356487,-0.06307917]','','2026-08-29 13:10:36.255141',NULL,'Land Act.pdf',40,'Land Act.pdf','0bf491dc352417899123f4c28c3c0e75c01f8c6ba3283b0ea9d4295731e64c38','',118),(831,94,'s Act or any\nother law.\n(8) Where a Committee has been appointed, it may, with the agreement of the parties to a dispute\nabout land, act as a Mediator in that dispute and when acting as a Mediator, a Committee shall have\nall the functions of a Mediator set out in section 89 of this Act and as may be prescribed.\n[section 64 substituted by section 27 of Act 1 of 2004]\n65. Qualification for appointment as member of a committee\n(1) A person shall qualify for appointment as a member of the committee if—\n(a) he or she is thirty years of age or more;\n(b) he or she has not been convicted of an offence involving moral turpitude; and\n(c) in the case of the chairperson, he or she is able to speak and write English.\n(2) At least one of the members referred to in section 64 shall be a woman.\n(3) At least one of the members referred to in section 64 shall be a person with knowledge and\nexperience in matters relating to land.\n66. Remuneration of members of committees\n(1) A member of the committee shall be paid such remuneration as may be determined by the district\ncouncil on the recommendation of the district executive committee.\n(2) All expenses incurred by or on behalf of the committee shall be charged on the district\nadministration funds.\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 35','68e12867abb34684adf4d997244b8b2018962d2095ae1c315b73d9526b8b4291','Land Act','General','[0.042107537,-0.06307715,-0.03319145,-0.0312694,-0.051405445,0.09774439,0.06431498,-0.039248418,-0.03549367,0.033308424,0.008484215,-0.06769148,0.010482844,-0.0060229907,-0.014329453,-0.024637697,0.038026623,0.03042638,-0.