returning officer shall declare as the elected chairperson, the candidate who has obtained the\nlargest number of votes cast.\n(2) The Electoral Commission shall ascertain, declare and publish in writing the results of a\nchairperson’s election within forty-eight hours from the close of polling.\n(3) A declaration executed by the Electoral Commission under subsection (2) and bearing the seal\nof the commission shall be evidence that the person named in the declaration has been elected\nchairperson of the relevant council.\n(4) Where two or more candidates tie in the leading position, the returning officer shall communicate\nthe results of the election to the Electoral Commission which shall arrange to have the elections\nrepeated.\n(5) The candidature for elections repeated under subsection (4) shall be limited to the candidates who\ntied in the first election.\n(6) No fresh nominations or candidates meeting shall be required for elections conducted under\nsubsection (4).\n(7) Subject to subsections (5) and (6), an election org','d5ed76b2c20abce6aae90ab1f60a0b2aec7f61ac23034fa0bef2b148f1621160','Local Governments Act','General','[-0.01366749,-0.008993085,0.06354602,-0.0014996874,-0.058648784,-0.011426326,-0.014251349,-0.0318699,-0.015663195,0.06533089,0.04065803,-0.059303526,0.011129487,-0.09390121,-0.004748267,-0.012311103,-0.02791854,0.0013402401,0.01459169,0.015407995,0.09902264,0.014615297,-0.018072646,-0.01397487,0.046435725,-0.06929267,-0.06275924,-0.026966179,0.030264776,-0.06435309,0.019702362,-0.05158369,0.02558696,-0.012350394,0.043850552,0.019699605,0.011223658,-0.021392751,0.04582725,-0.07950406,0.070303835,-0.054406047,-0.047229297,-0.11379507,-5.305152E-5,0.0076053916,0.01759351,-0.006958256,-0.06349219,-0.03119257,-0.015276605,-0.027000658,-0.012780864,-0.009551244,0.011476143,-0.027357887,-0.011574201,-0.05105907,0.004061664,0.0058231233,-0.0029770292,0.05815772,-0.16307378,0.011115647,0.017904663,-0.04357581,0.029763136,-0.119613364,0.047894437,0.00