trument, designate\nmagisterial areas and magistrates courts for the purposes of this Act.\n[section 2 substituted by section 2 of Act 6 of 2026]\n3. ***\n[section 3 repealed by section 3 of Act 6 of 2026]\n4. Appointment of magistrates\n(1) There shall be appointed such number of magistrates of such rank as the Chief Justice shall, in\nconsultation with the Judiciary Council and in accordance with the approved structure of the\nJudiciary, determine.\n(2) Magistrates shall be of the following ranks—\n(a) chief magistrate; and\n(b) magistrate.\n(3) The power and jurisdiction of a chief magistrate or magistrate shall be the powers and jurisdiction\nvested in the chief magistrate or magistrate under this Act and any other written law.\n[section 4 substituted by section 4 of Act 6 of 2026]\n5. Constitution of courts\n(1) A magistrate’s court shall be deemed to be duly constituted when presided over by any one\nmagistrate lawfully empowered to adjudicate in the court.\n6. Assignment of magistrates\nEvery magistrate appointed under this Act shall be deemed to have been appointed to, and have\njurisdiction in, each and every magisterial area but may be assigned to any particular magisterial area or to\na part of any magisterial area by the Chief Justice.\n7. Place of sitting\n(1) A magistrate’s court—\n(a) may be held at any place within the local limits of its jurisdiction; or\n(b) if it appears to the Chief Justice that the interests of justice so require, may be held, with the\nwritten authorisation of the Chief Justice, at a place outside the local','c06cb2d73e00d6efb369c39a508f6534bade96ab3f6eb327f8970cd01b0bba9d','Magistrates Courts Act','General','[0.02438308,-0.03387232,0.008667657,-0.070235655,-0.091570914,-0.044174947,0.0097719,0.010586098,-0.045114536,0.08559438,0.014094228,-0.05053396,0.03418435,-0.0506301,0.03721926,-4.571963E-4,-0.020738982,0.007944476,-0.051509365,0.0053120106,0.1077072,0.0010963866,0.00512811,-0.06298614,-0.08512294,-0.014513022,-0.10110829