ition for\nrevision can be made in the course of the proceedings.\nPart VI – Summons\n44. Form and contents of summons\n(1) Every summons issued by a magistrate’s court under this Act shall be in writing, in duplicate, signed\nand sealed by the magistrate or by such other officer as the Chief Justice may direct.\n(2) Every summons shall be directed to the person summoned and shall require him or her to appear at\na time and place to be appointed in the summons before a court having jurisdiction to inquire into\nand deal with the complaint or charge.\n(3) The summons shall state shortly the offence with which the person against whom the summons is\nissued, is charged.\n45. Service of summons\n(1) Every summons shall be served by a police officer or by an officer of the court issuing it or by other\npublic servant and shall, if practicable, be served personally on the person summoned by delivering\nor tendering to him or her the duplicate of the summons.\n(2) Every person on whom a summons is so served shall, if so required by the serving officer, sign for\nthe receipt of the summons on the back of the original summons.\n46. Service when person cannot','c06cb2d73e00d6efb369c39a508f6534bade96ab3f6eb327f8970cd01b0bba9d','Magistrates Courts Act','General','[-0.08240827,0.08076796,0.043944634,-0.07017948,-0.06960479,6.378342E-5,0.015252489,0.0050157933,0.013909814,0.06495927,0.032037694,-0.02580379,-7.6323387E-4,-0.08278413,-0.027794452,-0.022243196,0.0036323385,-0.007648607,-0.023422483,0.06615271,0.079636976,0.06908964,-0.030781684,-0.010491861,-0.028424129,0.042683117,-0.108821005,-0.033551477,0.08525087,-0.051789828,0.006320124,0.100142546,-0.020293081,-0.002968626,0.017298304,0.015741784,0.041268,-0.037564743,0.055090882,-0.11132305,0.05314387,-0.011597791,-0.007555661,-0.11454855,0.0037688145,0.018416785,0.018393267,0.02099148,-0.03517605,-0.018069366,-0.059853382,-0.084349476,-0.02193743,0.06323697,-0.031332113,-0.029249901,0.059580628,-0.009242292,0.02718777,-0.01