epositions taken under subsection (1) may, on the arrest of ich person, be given in evidence\nagainst him or her on the inquiry into or trial of the offence with which he or she is charged if the\ndeponent is dead or incapable of giving evidence, or his or her attendance cannot be procured\nwithout an amount of delay, expense or inconvenience which, under the circumstances of the case,\nwould be unreasonable.\n(3) If it appears that an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for a period of not less than\nseven years has been committed by some person or persons unknown, the High Court may direct\nthat a chief magistrate or a magistrate grade I shall hold an inquiry and examine any witnesses who\nca','c06cb2d73e00d6efb369c39a508f6534bade96ab3f6eb327f8970cd01b0bba9d','Magistrates Courts Act','General','[-0.09191264,0.11783436,0.026463512,-0.017514134,0.028851327,-0.017413579,0.054498915,-0.0050869966,-0.031228917,0.09570468,0.06212051,-0.100860015,0.015346333,0.019678658,-0.033128895,-0.0013230204,0.031364266,-0.01690568,-0.006437018,0.051863443,0.032954704,0.018728111,0.014940621,-0.026882047,-0.039464034,0.029154751,-0.07802018,-0.09421407,0.011302104,-0.025113255,0.010839441,0.04322045,0.013630885,0.0036488927,0.05561115,0.03370031,0.089751214,0.038833596,0.052142855,-0.004253906,0.007347832,-0.051694196,0.046228755,-0.11946523,-0.019080628,-0.00447476,0.076611824,0.04259255,-0.08759265,-0.024783283,-0.1058923,-0.08910591,0.0046739834,0.026735188,-0.02580737,-0.081793875,0.032503188,-0.018786795,0.006060251,-0.00330214,-0.030550309,0.027816536,-0.12073709,0.0033430385,0.042346172,-0.0024243356,0.048814747,-0.028037582,0.07868642,0.040114984,0.08272425,-0.018912628,0.03900888,-0.018859241,-0.07951452,-0.02578229,0.006301351,0.0041587763,0.009124594,-0.09475291,-0.0042391713,0.019018656,0.06987601,-0.07966307,0.039707765,-0.04025772,-0.05186527,0.011249945,0.037348267,-0.030644348,0.07252662,-0.034560475,4.5436536E-4,0.0152603015,0.09659129,-0.030844213,0.04478