f it is made before the accused person is called upon to make his or her defence, he or she shall\nbe discharged, but the discharge of an accused person shall not operate as a bar to subsequent\nproceedings against him or her on account of the same facts;\n(b) if it is made after the accused person is called upon to make his or her defence, he or she shall be\nacquitted.\n122. Adjournments\n(1) Before or during the hearing of any case, the court may adjourn the hearing if sufficient cause\nis shown, on due application made in open court for the adjournment; but when the hearing of\nevidence has first be','c06cb2d73e00d6efb369c39a508f6534bade96ab3f6eb327f8970cd01b0bba9d','Magistrates Courts Act','General','[-0.042517684,0.06758575,-0.027419928,-0.031116417,0.030115886,0.022079943,0.098618574,-0.042125415,0.05017622,-0.021266641,0.091764815,0.049837086,-0.019693442,-0.01869436,-0.028749483,-0.050334983,0.04642711,0.04723023,0.02173928,0.070914336,0.0037129887,-0.026189504,-0.01996319,-0.026029382,-0.05711865,0.011792403,-0.017486883,-0.048047166,-0.018935477,-0.010383599,0.0075260773,0.00944749,0.02035363,-0.034728352,0.0040652957,-0.019201053,0.004088475,-0.047837276,0.014237051,-0.042208605,0.01728835,8.25414E-4,-0.02876674,-0.046093952,0.0053270636,-0.02346583,-0.0397896,0.051238798,-0.049043503,-0.033017714,-0.062115964,-0.028262526,-0.018313292,0.08739018,-0.092823125,0.029202597,0.05496815,0.05016744,0.0013257989,0.060164332,-0.055181876,0.024438119,-0.06274344,0.020266738,0.0068405094,-0.0064798594,0.100233436,-0.008254761,0.112063035,0.07222734,-0.010426472,0.067268126,-0.021041809,-0.042456847,-0.09282359,-0.015016363,0.019024229,-0.04604753,0.026656782,-0.04604895,-0.025595678,-0.020125562,-0.028141527,-0.106152534,-0.01639389,-0.078962736,-0.02992372,-0.0107186325,0.06604841,-0.030340837,0.051856298,-0.008898111,-0.09495884,-0.006821582,0.049732458,0.009253961,-0.035279404,0.120153956,0.07473657,0.07707317,0.019398872,0.05698216,-0.06912281,-0.03209768,0.01