or personal injury in consequence of the offence committed and that\nsubstantial compensation is, in the opinion of the court, recoverable by that person by civil suit,\nthe court may, in its discretion and in addition to any other lawful punishment, order the convicted\nperson to pay to that other person such compensation as the court deems fair and reasonable.\n(2) When any person is convicted of any offence under Chapters XXIV to XXIX of the Penal Code Act,\nthe power conferred by subsection (1) shall be deemed to include a power to award compensation to\nany bona fide purchaser of any property in relation to which the offence was committed for the loss\nof that property if the property is restored to the possession of the person entitled to it.\n(3) Any order for compensation under this section shall be subject to appeal, and no payment of\ncompensation shall be made before the period allowed for presenting the appeal has elapsed or, if\nan appeal is presented, before the determination of the appeal.\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 52','c06cb2d73e00d6efb369c39a508f6534bade96ab3f6eb327f8970cd01b0bba9d','Magistrates Courts Act','General','[-0.05691793,0.110573165,-0.027332155,-0.013484623,0.079337925,0.07011765,0.14350225,0.07244494,0.025691984,0.058093425,0.0897069,-0.049245674,0.07521396,0.0442563,-0.05586997,-0.01412599,0.024445262,0.08998551,-0.051721912,0.049842548,0.0724702,-0.0031389676,0.006439042,-0.04617393,0.0076658996,-1.7828826E-5,-0.04663185,-0.053867616,0.024515018,-0.074965194,-0.047996745,0.041037824,-0.018522743,-0.037733722,3.620316E-4,0.0018545274,0.030281993,-0.041742448,-0.028714351,-0.0040480415,0.010311718,0.019479005,0.009155101,-0.071545206,-0.029371195,-0.041774943,0.10225888,0.07354473,-0.067880824,-0.024565527,-0.029000139,-0.04146994,-0.010709601,0.087577306,-0.034918852,-0.01759502,0.019036608,-0.014752038,-0.0016329808,0.06741893,0.00429348,-0.0038181546,-0.036635354,9.863075E-4,0.056053393,-0.029789492,0.0349