 If any person charged with any offence as is mentioned in Chapters XXIV to XXIX, of the Penal\nCode Act, in stealing, taking, obtaining, extorting, converting, or disposing of, or in knowingly\nreceiving any property is prosecuted to conviction or admits the offence under any of the provisions\nof this Act, the property shall be restored to the owner or the owner’s representative.\n(2) In every case referred to in this section, the court before which such offender is convicted shall have\npower to award orders for restitution for the property or to order the restitution of the property in a\nsummary manner; but—\n(a) where goods as defined in the Sale of Goods and Supply of Services Act have been obtained\nby fraud or other wrongful means not amounting to stealing, the property in such goods\nshall not revest in the person who was the owner of the goods, or his o','c06cb2d73e00d6efb369c39a508f6534bade96ab3f6eb327f8970cd01b0bba9d','Magistrates Courts Act','General','[-0.11384049,0.116677076,0.0023752137,-0.071387336,0.026250314,0.08112071,0.14390934,0.018639917,-0.015584111,0.06598329,0.1036169,-0.04080634,0.065386035,-0.07329241,-0.04276988,0.018577639,0.025453199,0.08711687,-0.032984085,0.052970935,0.073612705,0.053683173,-0.059271064,-0.016479248,0.02218533,-0.015588347,-0.0069076023,0.04743579,0.040175326,0.0057561668,-0.0026319847,0.010487363,0.0030868202,0.026040344,-0.03712978,0.048560742,0.031462632,-0.062111903,-0.024978234,-0.03411923,-0.022459587,0.0018372244,0.02080874,-0.081664234,0.054159917,0.0016631482,0.054866273,0.023686819,-0.059711207,-0.07506124,0.019538734,0.04674983,-0.022158021,0.06153248,-0.05081967,0.0042486303,0.059151765,-0.013254318,0.019509254,-0.02046774,0.018881364,0.017802365,-0.022436265,0.04913472,0.052377705,-0.036485586,-0.010997654,-0.019516211,0.016341768,0.038152006,0.10703174,-6.4896233E-4,0.02629215,-0.0025330342,-0.028394915,0.009815523,0.007653411,0.030947998,-0.07665196,-0.010292634,-0.0318797,-0.07043865,0.031645287,-0.0