ate dispersal given under section 33 shall be deemed to be an unlawful assembly within the\nmeaning of section 65 of the Penal Code Act.\n35. Gazetted areas\n(1) If the Minister is of the opinion that it is desirable in the interests of public tranquillity, he or she\nmay, by statutory instrument, declare that in any particular area in Uganda (hereafter referred to\nin this section as a “gazetted area”) it shall be unlawful for any person or persons to convene an\nassembly at which it is reasonable to suppose that more than twenty-five persons will be present\nunless a permit has been obtained under subsection (2) by that person or those persons to convene\nthe assembly, except that no instrument published under this subs','7fb225a86eeeb778016f2e266ca51c84753f2e5c72cfae7a53cf6a3117a6330c','Police Act','General','[-0.013456497,0.05177222,0.023268195,-0.008258479,-0.026169423,0.02357916,0.020318216,-0.08026301,-0.022295533,0.0677131,0.024453362,-0.008679714,-0.0021638388,0.0013385243,0.0063514514,-0.0275061,0.036109377,-0.003200375,-0.08673324,0.100935295,0.07944831,0.04393042,-0.015760977,0.07949208,-0.099207096,-0.008818071,-0.12102005,-0.020702895,0.092485435,-0.031688575,-0.0013073402,0.039450105,-0.048950456,0.013709001,0.058292694,-6.406915E-5,0.05215692,-0.046740998,0.062417053,-0.031434577,0.038468283,0.0052872472,0.013567367,-0.010394263,-0.009470022,0.028252624,0.017239887,0.005101684,-0.0608258,-0.0099679455,0.036186222,-0.031526715,-0.0115963835,0.05701481,-0.084642954,-0.043151364,0.019393213,-0.05913476,-0.0011487671,0.018422166,-0.08996405,0.07155243,-0.061162822,-0.016452357,0.02008894,-0.03485408,0.043034367,-0.029021274,0.05798404,0.05067829,0.051243514,-0.044973034,0.0045426856,0.041784436,-0.06992264,-0.054211676,-0.030206922,-0.057257686,-0.04264394,-0.12225195,-0.012625441,0.037764788,0.06567924,-0.035187572,-0.0017314813,-0.04535503,-0.041991297,0.048902035,0.06063132,0.045665838,-0.02483137,0.031515073,0.08767839,0.0023610657,0.07851987,-0.0050