 of\nthat property at the instance of any person claiming to be interested in it, and in all other cases where the\ndelegate considers that the property incurs any risk of loss or damage; and for that purpose, if he or she\nsees fit, to appoint an officer to take and keep possession of the property.\n236. When probate or administration may be granted by Chief Magistrate or Magistrate\nProbate of the will or letters of administration to the estate of a deceas person may be granted by the Chief\nMagistrate or Magistrate under the st of his or her court, if it appears by a petition, verified as hereafter\nprovide of the person applying for the probate or letters of administrat','627b160233ed70167530ad169ea5a5028257e7feaf909cd0722428b944bd41dc','Succession Act #U2014 Chapter 268','General','[-0.07299791,0.08683738,-0.043110263,-0.07955232,-0.018064914,0.047453262,0.0728319,-0.0025882337,0.01289346,0.08707589,0.10059845,-0.036496118,0.036145113,-0.03511888,0.010628531,0.0158405,0.06352301,-9.362901E-4,-0.07292622,0.0834316,0.11649522,0.027938353,1.2055245E-4,-0.008058236,-0.016953656,-0.068941034,-0.01000644,-0.059603427,0.053615306,-0.014466907,-0.017925097,-0.054636627,-0.05463293,0.03213921,0.035379462,0.00847378,-0.020745456,-0.05619834,-0.050095145,-0.0669736,-0.00821431,0.049021367,-0.0019237419,-0.039944787,0.054952186,0.0067879995,0.023877915,0.014478509,-0.08112321,-0.067315556,-0.006889462,-0.026325775,0.045632515,0.06938632,-0.04654247,-0.05407478,0.033291906,0.0148788495,-0.0061499695,-0.0187607,-0.05947035,-0.009568473,-0.039511405,-0.040672727,-0.00602347,-0.0186063,0.05017388,-0.017626759,-0.010538621,0.0347572,0.07315795,-0.0033956503,0.056730438,0.06458058,-0.07093275,-0.03888522,-0.014049876,0.023658011,-0.015479837,-0.10852631,0.045930862,-0.0032927047,0.03094337,-0.07978651,-0.032312054,-0.036660906,-0.03127155,0.014413287,0.12163726,0.06433629,0.020271476,-0.05499618,0.063348904,-0.023244686,0.022144476,0.029858226,0.0014321653,-0.048829604,0.0496106