ne country to be its ambassador, consul or other\nrepresentative in another country does not acquire a domicile in the latter country by reason only of\nresiding there in pursuance of the appointment, nor does any other person acquire such domicile by\nreason only of residing with that person as part of his or her family or as a servant.\n9. Continuance of new domicile\nA new domicile continues until the former domicile has been resumed or another has been acquired.\n10. Domicile of origin of child\n(1) The domicile of a child follows the domicile of the parent of the child or the guardian of the child\nfrom whom the child derives his or her domicile of origin.\n(2) Where the parents of a child have different domicile, the domicile of the child shall follow the\ndomicile of the parent who has custody of the child.\n11. Domicile of choice\n(1) A person may upon marriage, acquire the domicile of his or her spouse.\n(2) A spouse may upon dissolution of a marriage or upon judicial separation or any other separation\nrecognised under the laws of Uganda, acquire any other domicile.\n12. Acquisition of new domicil','627b160233ed70167530ad169ea5a5028257e7feaf909cd0722428b944bd41dc','Succession Act — Chapter 268','General','[-0.028292982,0.012714609,0.047427133,-0.06944776,-0.061699703,-0.056874674,-0.003766026,-0.029655054,0.033977773,0.044236068,0.05987915,-0.012681025,0.03619408,-0.015339463,0.0036702752,-0.014694412,-0.032415446,0.0041767093,-0.042261247,0.09174059,0.0666732,-0.013076355,0.0016764058,-0.031897366,0.022880571,-0.037906453,-0.007911285,-0.04186006,0.14613304,-0.013876896,0.07891769,0.022390049,-0.046898786,0.024782121,0.026148561,0.07019456,-0.018571349,0.021860477,0.049052212,-0.0557874,0.10798486,-0.05700232,0.074578576,-0.12373493,-0.0022500732,-0.016140284,0.05347273,-0.008014368,-0.076728895,-0.033026878,-0.03711951,-0.05682912,0.008354539,0.11082943,-0.060854174,0.035011556,0.040873174,-0.074066885,0.02559887,-0.021243943,0.008652337,0.064415984,-0.0