336) ...................................................','Succession Act — Chapter 268.pdf',16,'Succession Act — Chapter 268.pdf','d2b36864ee32804ae5741fa42fb015719b5011eb8c86b74aaf38fc82fccc90ea','',190),(1944,53,'use.\n(2) A spouse may upon dissolution of a marriage or upon judicial separation or any other separation\nrecognised under the laws of Uganda, acquire any other domicile.\n12. Acquisition of new domicile by minor\nExcept as provided in section 13, a person cannot during minority acquire a new domicile.\n13. Acquisition of new domicile by mentally impaired person\nA mentally impaired person cannot acquire a new domicile in any other way than by his or her domicile\nfollowing the domicile of another person.\n14. Succession to movable property in Uganda\nWhere a deceased leaves movable property in Uganda, succession to the property shall, in the absence of\nproof of any domicile elsewhere, be regulated by the laws of Uganda.\nPart III – Consanguinity\n15. Kindred or consanguinity\nKindred or consanguinity is the connection or relation of persons descended from the same stock or\ncommon ancestor.\nBy Ulii.org and Laws.Africa. Share widely and freely. 3','627b160233ed70167530ad169ea5a5028257e7feaf909cd0722428b944bd41dc','Succession Act — Chapter 268','General','[-0.05149349,0.05398774,-0.030103505,-0.02595469,-0.037940852,-0.018434431,8.019219E-4,-0.06967365,0.009825201,0.036662195,0.10224693,0.014428107,0.053102117,-0.012670926,-0.00682696,-0.002936392,-0.020364022,0.020265525,-0.13456233,0.10246554,0.018689072,0.017981518,-0.0060935887,-0.024392141,0.055813547,-0.019710375,-0.012340558,-0.020458793,0.12591507,-0.02448734,0.04708144,0.058593966,-0.046588097,0.049263056,0.0045794626,0.02026998,-0.040866327,0.061388012,0.06497645,-0.03624761,0.024185423,-0.0471817,0.07860699,-0.070884846,-0.03662959,0.015802631,0.014959592,0.009950239,-0.03757497,-0.028465718,-0.06603165,-0.036370732,-0.010718467,0.15746072,-0.020884745,0.034792945,-0.019944146,-0.031024188,-