ing.\n89. Voting in Parliament.\n(1) Except as otherwise prescribed by this Constitution or any law\nconsistent with this Constitution, any question proposed for decision of\nParliament shall be determined by a majority of votes of the members present\nand voting in a manner prescribed by rules of procedure made by Parliament\nunder article 94 of this Constitution.\n(2) The person presiding in Parliament shall have neither an original\nnor a casting vote and if on any question before Parliament the votes are\nequally divided, the motion shall be lost.\n90. Committees of Parliament.\n(1) Parliament shall appoint standing committees and other\ncommittees necessary for the efficient discharge of its functions.','5b61e676e218c67447284dbefc988bf1aeaf087d564b594fc8271fc20061ebe8','Uganda Constitution 1995','General','[-0.027226588,0.01488997,-0.016231509,-0.07959441,-0.14977664,0.023147183,0.02802576,0.016888525,-0.026932763,0.08922492,-0.034978293,-0.010767026,0.044984624,-0.03754929,-0.016476607,0.005088917,0.040687133,-0.016568623,0.008724613,0.102950506,0.028645366,0.004860504,-0.09666439,0.015904754,-0.05538624,-0.06706094,-0.006297954,0.0042217034,0.010176238,-0.034947865,-0.012435905,-0.050835393,0.09276341,0.05539589,0.07088127,-0.062167693,0.087992206,-0.107048556,0.03782479,-0.014169711,0.032389015,-0.051348075,-0.114100486,-0.025123958,0.030256817,0.007985804,-7.554532E-4,0.009921055,-0.12254726,-0.013333405,-0.09646629,-0.008862673,-0.03512933,0.026907617,0.020140994,-0.03997504,0.006612927,-0.041704185,0.07409813,-0.066176556,-0.121244304,-0.0023836351,-0.0033290056,0.04951573,0.024014868,-0.048140004,0.0034147243,-0.08158251,0.05150632,0.029623091,-0.030792223,0.009839489,0.0077137067,-0.053747088,-0.13366312,-0.10939225,-0.014248191,0.040568195,0.015513131,-0.041194692,0.0011848595,0.025478495,-0.012148588,-0.056008693,0.032118067,-0.101115495,-0.006522239,0.017432721,0.014607043,-0.002164112,-0.04523277,0.025342729,0.013060427,-0.04194035,0.011981498,0.016