he approval of Parliament.\n(3) A Cabinet Minister shall have responsibility for such functions of\nGovernment as the President may, from time to time, assign to him or her.\n(4) A Minister shall not hold any office of profit or emolument likely\nto compromise his or her office.\n114. Other Ministers.\n(1) The President may, with the approval of Parliament, appoint other\nMinisters to assist Cabinet Ministers in the performance of their functions.\n(2) Subject to the provisions of this article, article 113(1) of this\nConstitution shall apply to the appointment of Ministers under clause (1) of\nthis article.\n(3) The total number of Ministers appointed under this article shall\nnot exceed twenty-one except with the approval of Parliament.\n(4) A Minister referred to in this article shall have responsibility for\nsuch functions of the Ministry to which he or she is appointed as the','5b61e676e218c67447284dbefc988bf1aeaf087d564b594fc8271fc20061ebe8','Uganda Constitution 1995','General','[0.010212694,-0.031659294,-0.009904842,-0.046534754,-0.061838455,-0.011965075,-0.027054831,-0.02627189,0.02686045,0.038165804,-0.038585905,-0.02547064,0.04164498,-0.027782923,0.013483459,-0.048167624,0.013850657,0.06663828,-0.054834533,-0.019915385,0.0969619,0.006656126,-0.029733235,-0.054339997,-0.08970894,-0.095186815,-0.062680006,-0.087142274,-0.012649937,0.006471456,0.01574227,-0.09043583,0.008904462,-0.02299887,0.013521842,0.02203078,0.049250554,-0.004908174,0.056207925,-0.020478336,-0.0061354577,-0.026270203,-0.0420285,-0.050349038,0.008276408,-0.026718212,0.023965323,0.011568277,-0.0685067,-0.08089656,-0.016651336,0.042749945,-0.06290472,0.033564515,-0.03945879,0.03940276,0.014020014,-0.1239509,0.03014417,0.021451563,-0.07253934,0.0045252657,-0.05641966,0.028882293,-0.031822704,0.021768492,-0.0049366844,-0.009319227,0.020413065,0.04051455,-0.03538038,-0.03519293,0.01245491,0.0038259956,-0.070225514,-0.061947785,-0.03220198,0.08452179,0.016830485,-0.06545313,-0.034694653,0.120285